  "title": "Battle of Ayacucho",
  "summary": "On 9 December 1824, near Quinua close to Huamanga, a patriot army under Antonio José de Sucre defeated the royalist forces of Viceroy José de la Serna, who was captured. The royalists capitulated that day, ending Spanish military power in Peru and effectively South America; Callao held out until 1826.",
